# Chapter 01 independent full meaning review

No blocking finding. Direct full reading compares the fixed afeadcf70b120c7cf05e48ec2c282e0e4edd5e44 Markdown and authored Doc, authoring.md, AGENTS and the declared dependency catalog. This is a new review of the whole chapter, not merely acceptance of the author's preflight or previous review. Source SHA-256 f5024444c85b45094874a961d52da111798ed37efa6c40fa0954c8caaf7c4170; Doc SHA-256 8d338b3ce98f3030e503ecd0aea9374c439c606cfbeb48bcd6b777a3f45654b2. All fixed context files equal the named main commit and are saved.

- Policy: initial monorepo, matching semantic/crate boundaries, separated languages/backends and dependencies.json as the complete permission set are preserved. The added phrase-level Anno defines dependency direction as consumer to dependency, exactly supported by section 2; it is not a translation or altered permission.
- Layout: the full directory tree, language paths, foundation/domain/output/integration/UI/app/web/site/editor/tool/example/conformance/task entries and spacing/newlines are retained as non-evaluated RawCode. Filename hierarchy is still directories, with source_span_map.rs versus source/map.rs and src containing lib.rs or main.rs. The tree is explicitly a target layout, not a claim every path exists.
- Dependency directions: the second RawCode retains every original edge and inline qualifier byte-for-byte, including math-tex, suite domain/backend dependencies, wire, UI data-only core dependency, web UI edge and tools. Both RawCode language hints are exactly text. No Markdown table or semantic list exists to omit; apparent column/list structure belongs to these exact code blocks. The source's diagram is a principal-direction summary, not a replacement for the complete dependencies.json allowlist.
- Boundaries: core owns typed schema/positions/diagnostics/public values, not all domain enums; domain cores lower common parsed trees, engine does not know Doc/Ruby semantics. Suite bridges bidirectional Doc/Math embeds; doc-core does not import math-core, backends do not import each other, and resolved typed fragments follow dependency preparation. Pure UI owns Model/Msg/update/view/command/subscription descriptions, while host owns execution/Worker/widgets. Target 20 crates and 15 no_std + alloc crates match the catalog; implemented member counts are expressly separate. Explicit tool-side documentation generation and prohibition of compiler/renderer build.rs cycles remain.
- Bootstrap: each syntax.neplg defines the surface, checked packages are committed, normal builds do not gain compiler/tools build dependencies, and the exact cargo generate check command is preserved. Grammar seed represents the same grammar rather than a miniature alternate dialect; compile/semantic-normal-form seed comparison and persistent future bootstrap use are retained.
- Rust: edition 2024, resolver 3, MSRV at least 1.85.0 versus a separately exact-pinned stable development toolchain, centralized dependencies and committed lock remain. Core stays no_std with alloc and has no std-enabling feature; std adapters belong outside core and metadata/target builds detect contamination. All four num-* crate names, default-features=false, mutually resolved/locked versions, no cross-language exposed BigInt versions and canonical integer/rational public values remain. Safe Rust default, adapter-local necessary unsafe with contracts/tests and no external domain pointers remain.
- Verification/extraction: production/build versus separately reported dev edges, forbidden production-to-apps/tools/domain-to-domain/cycles/std paths, external OS contamination checks and independent no-default-features checks are preserved. Repository splitting is not forced prematurely; replacement occurs by public schema/operation. The one real Relative link is 22-external-extensions.md, without a fragment, labelled 外部拡張契約. Monorepo remains current while independent workspace API evidence precedes distribution/provider/compatibility work.
- Current stage: all preceding architecture is a target; actual Cargo.toml and implementation-status.json remain authoritative for present members/implementation. Responsibility-based crate addition and the two original development/ADR text references remain. No runtime completion or real repository split is newly claimed.

All eight heading meanings and all prose paragraphs were read against their counterparts. Natural paraphrases change punctuation and phrasing without dropping requirements. Sentence literals divide ordinary prose into sentences; inline code-bearing sentences and the real link use explicit construction. Kanji-only Ruby and okurigana separation were read throughout, including 埋/う + め + 込/こ + み, 解決済/かいけつず + み, 依存方向/いぞんほうこう and 版番号/はんばんごう. The only explanatory Anno is the supported dependency-direction note. There is no artificial translation or parallel requirement. RawCode is correctly exempt from adding Ruby inside original code bytes.

